{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgS2Z5XJzhDFk8aM88dX6","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I split the system prompt into two blocks in `build_system` (`bot.py`), so a `save_fact` no longer invalidates the static instructions. I haven't tested it, since I can't call the API from here.\n\n**Cause:** The instructions and the athlete context (today's date plus the facts list) were one text block with one cache breakpoint. `save_fact` changes the facts, so the whole block changed and the cached prefix was thrown away.\n\n**Change:** The `INSTRUCTIONS` block now has its own breakpoint. The athlete context is a separate block after it with a second breakpoint. A fact write now only changes the second block.\n\n**It may not show up in the logs.** Sonnet 4.5 only caches prefixes of at least 1024 tokens. By my rough estimate (character counts and the log), the tools plus instructions come to about 900 tokens. If so, that part is too small to cache on its own. After a `save_fact`, check `cache_read_input_tokens` in `logs/usage.jsonl`. If it's still 0, the static part needs to grow past 1024 tokens.\n\n**The tool filter also breaks the cache.** Tools come before the system prompt in the cached prefix. When `select_tools` adds a group such as `plan_week`, the tools list changes and the cache misses. The log shows this too: those rounds have 0 cache reads. I left the filter alone, as `NOTES.md` says. If you want to fix that too, you could send a fixed tool list, or measure whether the filter's token savings outweigh the cache misses.\n\n`ANSWER.md` has the same write-up."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1598,"cache_read_input_tokens":26176,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1598},"output_tokens":518,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standa